EXPOSE
EXPOSE 3000
This tells Docker:
"This containerized application normally listens on port 3000."

But important:

EXPOSE itself does NOT publish the port to your host.

If Node server:

app.listen(3000);

and Dockerfile:

EXPOSE 3000

still browser-la:

localhost:3000
automatically work aagathu.

Need:

docker run -p 3000:3000 my-app

Meaning:

Host             Container
3000      →      3000

So:

EXPOSE
= documentation / metadata about intended port

-p
= actual host-to-container port publishing
This distinction interview-la kooda useful.